id: pm-gactwj
title: Broad squash commits overflow hosted-analysis tree lookup and falsely lose reviewed PR provenance
description: "The hosted analysis gate reads each commit through the heavyweight REST commits endpoint using spawnSync with Node default buffering. PR #1133 merged a 105-file squash whose response exceeds that buffer, so the subprocess terminates with status null and the gate treats the merge tree as unavailable even though GitHub associates PR #1133 and the merge/head trees are identical."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 0
tags[6]: analyzer-provenance,"area:ci","area:release",defect-escape,github-actions,regression
created_at: "2026-08-28T15:09:32.562Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-28T15:38:18.283Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-28T15:38:17.671Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-28T15:38:17.671Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "The gate requests commit tree metadata from a narrow immutable endpoint whose payload does not scale with changed-file patches; A focused negative regression proves the old heavyweight lookup would overflow while the new lookup resolves the exact tree; Fail-closed behavior for missing or malformed tree metadata remains intact; Focused tests, exact 100/100/100/100 repository coverage, static quality, manual temporary-directory acceptance, exact-head PR review, merged-main analyzer readiness, and release gates pass"
definition_of_ready: "Production failure, exact merge/head/tree evidence, buffer root cause, canonical lineage, and no-duplicate all-status search are recorded."
goal: project management = context management
objective: Make reviewed-PR analyzer provenance deterministic for arbitrarily broad squash commits without increasing unbounded subprocess buffering.
value: Broad SDK and CLI deliveries can pass the mandatory merged-main analyzer readiness gate and proceed to immutable release without weakening provenance.
impact: "The only failed job on merged-main CI run 33182695715 blocks the 2026.8.28 release despite every product, coverage, static, compatibility, smoke, and Windows job passing."
outcome: "Commit tree lookup uses a bounded Git database endpoint, retains fail-closed behavior, and has a regression test that prevents large standard commit payloads from reintroducing false provenance loss."
why_now: PR #1133 is merged and release-ready except for this production defect; release must remain blocked until a reviewed fix passes exact-main CI.
parent: pm-u9d0
risk: high
confidence: high
severity: high
environment: GitHub Actions hosted runner; unbraind/pm-cli main merge 0480ab6668d2699acc63558acf99c02bd3b5a571; CI run 33182695715 job 98887669749; Node spawnSync; GitHub REST API
repro_steps: "Run scripts/release/hosted-analysis-gate.mjs for merge 0480ab6668d2699acc63558acf99c02bd3b5a571. The PR association resolves to #1133 and head 9f56a49524ae14d34e4a7c39370739bf2c4e2e9e; both git trees are 54f43f0400fcf0af653053cad1253cec7ca0ace1, but repos/unbraind/pm-cli/commits/<merge> exceeds spawnSync default maxBuffer and readCommitTree returns null."
resolution: Use the Git Database commit endpoint to read immutable tree metadata without file/patch expansion; preserve malformed/unavailable fail-closed behavior and prove the old response-size failure with a regression control.
expected_result: A reviewed squash merge with an identical reviewed head tree satisfies analyzer provenance regardless of the number of changed files.
actual_result: "The standard commits endpoint emits more than one MiB of file and patch data; spawnSync returns status null, readCommitTree returns null, and the gate reports no exact or identical-tree reviewed evidence."
affected_version: 2026.8.28
fixed_version: 2026.8.28
component: release automation / hosted analysis provenance
regression: true
customer_impact: "No broken artifact was published, but the valid daily SDK/CLI release is blocked until provenance lookup is repaired."
