comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-28T15:09:32.562Z","harness:codex","Duplicate-check and production evidence 2026-08-28: inspected all-status searches for the exact title, ENOBUFS, maxBuffer, and hosted-analysis commit-tree provenance; no item owns this broad-squash failure. Canonical pm-u1baah is closed with shipped analyzer-provenance behavior, so this item records a recurrence instead of reopening or duplicating that completed work. GitHub associates merge 0480ab6668d2699acc63558acf99c02bd3b5a571 with PR #1133 head 9f56a49524ae14d34e4a7c39370739bf2c4e2e9e, both trees equal 54f43f0400fcf0af653053cad1253cec7ca0ace1, and instrumentation shows the heavyweight commit request exits with null status after exceeding the default spawnSync buffer."
  "2026-08-28T15:11:07.905Z","harness:codex","TDD red evidence: changed the existing identical-tree squash regression to expose only the bounded Git commit metadata endpoint while simulating the standard commits endpoint overflowing at 1,048,577 bytes with null subprocess status. The focused test failed exactly at provenance resolution: expected identical_tree_squash_pr_head but received the fail-closed exact_commit refusal. No product code changed before this red control."
  "2026-08-28T15:27:12.607Z","harness:codex","Implementation and verification evidence: readCommitTree now uses repos/{repository}/git/commits/{sha} and validates tree.sha. The existing squash-provenance test simulates the old standard endpoint returning null status after a 1,048,577-byte response and requires exactly two bounded Git metadata reads. Focused suite passed 120/120. The real production control for merge 0480ab6668d2699acc63558acf99c02bd3b5a571 now passes as identical_tree_squash_pr_head at reviewed head 9f56a49524ae14d34e4a7c39370739bf2c4e2e9e with DeepScan and CodeFactor zero findings. Build, typecheck, repository static quality, graph composition, record integrity, SDK surface/import-cost/transport gates, and canonical coverage passed: 585 files, 8,088 tests, statements 60,000/60,000, branches 45,190/45,190, functions 12,477/12,477, lines 57,779/57,779. PM-linked tests passed 3/3, including isolated package-first dogfood in /tmp with 88 commands. npm reports pm-changelog 2026.8.22 as latest; project package doctor reports the managed package surface separately."
  "2026-08-28T15:28:17.490Z","harness:codex","Delivery: PR #1139 https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/1139 carries the bounded Git commit metadata fix at implementation commit 9f72d4203. Exact-head hosted checks and full bot review are pending; the item intentionally remains in progress until those proofs are terminal, after which closure, structured gate evidence, and generated changelog will be added to the same PR."
  "2026-08-28T15:38:17.063Z","harness:codex","Exact-head hosted evidence: PR #1139 head 9f72d42038e5d63f08ffd84fb71a274ae47e2981 passed every terminal check, including static, exact coverage, four coverage shards, typecheck, compatibility, smokes, Windows, runtime matrices, Docs and Skills, CodeQL, Semgrep, DeepScan 0 new, CodeFactor 0 findings, Trivy, TruffleHog, ShellCheck, PSScriptAnalyzer, actionlint, CodSpeed, and benchmarks. Greptile reported 5/5 with no actionable finding; CodeRabbit full review generated no actionable comments. Every bot comment/review was reacted to and individually acknowledged; Sourcery budget unavailability is recorded as a limitation, not approval. Review threads: zero."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-28T15:27:12.046Z","harness:codex","GitHub REST endpoints with equivalent-looking commit identities have materially different payload growth: repos/{owner}/{repo}/commits/{ref} expands files and patches, while repos/{owner}/{repo}/git/commits/{sha} returns bounded immutable commit metadata. Buffered subprocess consumers should choose the narrowest endpoint rather than raising maxBuffer, because broad reviewed deliveries are a normal production input."
